# fold-fragments.map -- where scripts/docs/fold-fragments.sh files a config fragment
# whose key prefix has no "## <prefix>" section of that exact name in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
#
# One rule per line: <key prefix><TAB><exact text of a "## " heading in docs/CONFIGURATION.md>.
# The longest matching prefix (whole dotted segments) wins. Blank lines and lines starting
# with # are ignored. The heading must exist: `fold-fragments.sh --check` fails on a rule
# whose heading is gone.
#
# Placement order for docs/configuration.d/<key with dots as __>.md (first hit wins):
#   1. the section of a heading (any level) that names the key's parent in backticks, the
#      longest parent first (`storage.database`, then `storage`);
#   2. the "## <heading>" this file maps the key's prefix to;
#   3. the "## <first segment of the key>" section (## storage, ## security, ...).
# Anything else is an error: add a rule here instead of letting the fold guess.
purge	soft_delete & purge
soft_delete	soft_delete & purge
audit	audit.siem
